  "texts": {
    "preamble": "S.Dipesh Bohra vs The Food Safety Officer on 19 February, 2025 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Crl.O.P In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 19.02.2025 Coram The Hon'Ble Mr.JUSTICE G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Crl.O.P.No.1526 of 2023 And Crl.M.P.Nos.866 & 867 of 2023 1.S.Dipesh Bohra 2.S.Prakash Chand .. Vs. The Food Safety Officer Coimbatore Corporation Section, Code No. 555 Food Safety and Drug Administration Department 219, Race Course Road Coimbatore - 641 018 .. Criminal Original Petition filed under Section 482 Cr.P.C. to records and quash the proceedings in S.T.C.No.373 of 2020 on the file of Judicial Magistrate Court No.I, Coimbatore insofar as the petitioners. For Petitioners : Mr.M.Rajaraman For Respondent : Mr.K.M.D.Muhilan Government Advocate (Crl. side)",
    "facts": "2. The case of the prosecution is that on 21.12.2018, the complainant gone to Suhani corporation at No. 354, Theppakula Veedi - 1, Coimbatore with an intention to take samples and at that time, the first accused was selling food items in his shop to the general public. The complainant enquired about Processed Papaya Soaked in Sugar Syrup to the first accused and had taken samples of the said produce and sent the same to the food analyst on 21.12.2018 and the Analyst tested the product from 24.12.2018 ot 16.08.2019 and sent a report on 21.08.2019 stating that sample had added color exceed the defined limit is unsafe. The designated officer sent a letter stating that the product had already lost its expiry. The complainant had sought for permission to file case against the accused to S.Dipesh Bohra vs The Food Safety Officer on 19 February, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/179998990/ 1 the designated officer and the same was granted by the commissioner of Food Safety and hence, he filed the above complaint before the learned Judicial Magistrate No.I, Coimbatore under the Section 59(i) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and 190(1)(A) and 200 CPC. Hence, the petitioner filed this petition to quash the said complaint. Considering the submissions made on either side, the fact the Food analyst given a report that the sample is unsafe.",
